{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Auto-Poll CI Status",
  "description": "Automatically checks the status of the remote CI pipeline Actions after a push and opens remediation tasks for any detected failures via GitHub MCP integration. if polling for status to steblize, wailt at least 1 minute between polls.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "agentStop"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Check the status of the remote CI pipeline workflow using the GitHub MCP only (if fails try additional 1-2 times), status should be tracked with respect to action done (e.g. lint fix check lint results, test fail check it passes etcw...). if there is a repeated error that prevents knowing the workflow status stop you activity. continue polling until the workflow is comletete (successfully or not. wait at least 2 minutes between polling intervals using 'sleep 120' command. If any failures are detected, immediately create a task to fix the identified error without waiting for user intervention. Focus on: 1) Retrieving the latest workflow run status, 2) Analyzing any failure logs or error messages to find the specific test/file or any item with a problem from Actions logs, 3) Creating a specific remediation task with error details and suggested fixes, 4) Prioritizing the task for immediate attention. 4) once no workflow is activley running - stop monitoring.\n\nconnect using MCP and find the exact issue before stating to fix it (if there is an issue):\n\ntypical workflow run times (time of each step, not cuumulated): \nstart -> free diskspace 3m\ninstallations 2m\ntype checking 1 m\nunit testing 25-35m\nproperty based tests - 5m\nBuild, tag, and push image to Amazon ECR - 6-8m\nscan docker image - \nother - less than 30 sec each\n"
  },
  "workspaceFolderName": "drawings",
  "shortName": "ci-status-monitor"
}